Package: dash
Type: Package
Title: Depth-Aware Structural-Zero and Hellinger Test for Microbiome Differential Abundance
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Yiqian", "Zhang", email = "zhang.16383@osu.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A two-part differential abundance test for microbiome count data.
    DASH combines a structural-zero prevalence score test, derived from a
    per-taxon zero-inflated Tobit model, with a weighted abundance test on
    Hellinger-Riemann intrinsic coordinates (HRIC) that uses an HC3 sandwich standard
    error and a robust affine bias correction. The two arms are combined per
    taxon by a Bonferroni min-P rule and by a Cauchy rule.
